{
  "borough": "Harrow",
  "application_type": "Householder",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;span lang=&quot;EN-US&quot; style=&quot;&quot;&gt;The&lt;/span&gt;\r\nproposed development, by reason of its siting in&amp;nbsp;a surface water flood zone,\r\nFlood Zone’s 2 and 3 and a Critical Drainage Area, in&lt;span lang=&quot;EN-US&quot; style=&quot;&quot;&gt; the absence of an adequate\r\nFlood Risk Assessment to assess the future impacts and provide adequate\r\nmitigation measures,&amp;nbsp; would be likely to result in the displacement of\r\nwater onto adjacent land and fail to provide resilience to flooding, to the detriment\r\nof the safety of future occupiers of the application site and adjacent sites,\r\ncontrary to&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;Policies\r\nS1 12 and SI 13 of the London Plan (2021), Policy CS1.U of the Harrow Core\r\nStrategy (2012), and &amp;nbsp;Policies DM9 and DM10 of the Development Management\r\nPolicies Local Plan document (2013).&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;The\r\nproposed ground floor rear extension, by reason of its excessive height, would give rise to an overbearing, unneighbourly and\r\nvisually obtrusive form of development which would result in an unacceptable\r\nimpact on the amenities of 96 Becmead Avenue. The proposed development would\r\nthereby be contrary to the National Planning Policy Framework (2024), Policy D3.D (7) of the London Plan (2021), Policy DM1 of the Development Management\r\nPolicies Local Plan document (2013) and the relevant provisions of the adopted\r\nSupplementary Planning Document: Residential Design Guide (2010).&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
